        "title": "Counting Basics and the Twelvefold Way",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Everything in enumerative combinatorics grows from **two rules** — sum and\nproduct. Layer selection on top (ordered/unordered × with/without repetition)\nand you get the four fundamental counts. Generalize \"select k from n\" to \"place\nk balls in n boxes\" and you arrive at the **twelvefold way**, Gian-Carlo Rota's\nunifying frame for elementary counting."
    }
